---
/**
 * The positioning, as a comparison: three ways to get a Claude Code window on a
 * Mac, and what each one actually runs.
 *
 * Every statement about another product is from its vendor's own page, as the
 * 2026-10-21 competitive brief graded them (P): Claude's desktop docs for the
 * first column, OpenAI's Codex import page for the second. They are dated in the
 * footnote because both products move; a claim here that stops being true is a
 * claim about someone else's product, so re-check them with each brief and drop
 * a column rather than leave it stale.
 *
 * Not a "versus" table with ticks and crosses. The two other apps are good at
 * what they are for; the point is only what each one runs.
 */
import { ANTHROPIC_TERMS } from "../config";
import SectionHeader from "./SectionHeader.astro";

const SOURCES = {
  desktop: "https://code.claude.com/docs/en/desktop",
  codexImport: "https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/import",
};

const COLUMNS = [
  {
    name: "Claude desktop app",
    runs: "Its own copy of Claude Code",
    lines: [
      "Its own session list: a session started in a terminal or VS Code is not in it",
      "Customisations synced through claude.ai, not read from ~/.claude",
    ],
    source: SOURCES.desktop,
    ours: false,
  },
  {
    name: "Codex in the ChatGPT app",
    runs: "Codex, with a copy of your Claude Code setup",
    lines: [
      "Imports your instructions, settings, skills, hooks, subagents and recent chats into its own format",
      "Keeps the copy in sync, as long as automatic updates are on",
      "Runs Codex, not Claude Code",
    ],
    source: SOURCES.codexImport,
    ours: false,
  },
  {
    name: "Drakar",
    runs: "The claude and codex you installed",
    lines: [
      "Over their own protocols, stream-json and app-server, the way the VS Code extension drives claude",
      "Reads ~/.claude and every ~/.claude-* account as they are; nothing is imported or synced",
      "Sessions from your terminal and VS Code show in the sidebar, and can move into the window",
    ],
    source: null,
    ours: true,
  },
] as const;
---

<section id="yours" class="relative scroll-mt-20 py-[104px]">
  <div class="wrap flex flex-col gap-12">
    <SectionHeader
      eyebrow="Yours, not a copy"
      heading="Nothing to import. Nothing to sync. Nothing bundled."
      class="mb-0!"
    >
      Drakar ships no agent. It runs the <code class="font-mono text-[0.9em] text-fg">claude</code> you
      installed (Settings › General picks which, when you have several) and talks to it the way
      Anthropic's own VS Code extension does. Your settings, skills, hooks, MCP servers and transcripts stay exactly
      where Claude Code keeps them, and a session you start in Drakar is one you can resume from a
      terminal.
    </SectionHeader>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 lg:grid-cols-3">
      {
        COLUMNS.map((c) => (
          <div
            class:list={[
              "reveal relative flex flex-col gap-4 overflow-hidden rounded-[16px] border p-6",
              c.ours
                ? "border-accent/40 bg-linear-to-b from-accent/[.10] to-bg-2 shadow-[0_30px_70px_-40px_rgba(130,100,255,.7)]"
                : "border-rule bg-bg-2",
            ]}
          >
            {c.ours && <div class="rim-plate absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-px" aria-hidden="true" />}
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
              <h3 class="m-0 text-[15px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.01em] text-fg">{c.name}</h3>
              {c.source && (
                <a
                  href={c.source}
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener"
                  class="font-mono text-[10.5px] text-fg-muted transition-colors hover:text-accent-hi"
                >
                  source ↗
                </a>
              )}
            </div>
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
              <span class="mono">Runs</span>
              <span
                class:list={[
                  "font-display text-[21px] leading-[1.2] font-semibold tracking-[-0.025em] text-balance",
                  c.ours ? "text-plate" : "text-fg",
                ]}
              >
                {c.runs}
              </span>
            </div>
            <ul class="m-0 flex list-none flex-col gap-2.5 p-0">
              {c.lines.map((line) => (
                <li class="flex gap-2.5 text-[13.5px] leading-[1.55] text-pretty text-fg-dim">
                  <span
                    class:list={[
                      "mt-[7px] block size-[5px] flex-none rounded-full",
                      c.ours ? "bg-accent" : "bg-fg-muted/60",
                    ]}
                    aria-hidden="true"
                  />
                  {line}
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <figure class="reveal m-0 flex flex-col gap-3 border-l-2 border-accent/60 pl-5 md:pl-7">
      <blockquote
        class="m-0 font-display text-[clamp(19px,2.2vw,25px)] leading-[1.4] font-medium tracking-[-0.02em] text-pretty text-fg"
      >
        “…{ANTHROPIC_TERMS.quote}.”
      </blockquote>
      <figcaption class="text-[13.5px] leading-[1.6] text-fg-muted">
        Anthropic's legal and compliance page, on who may use a Claude subscription with Claude Code.
        That sentence describes Drakar exactly: your subscription, your sign-in, the binary Anthropic
        ships. <a
          href={ANTHROPIC_TERMS.url}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="text-fg-dim underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-accent-hi">Read it there ↗</a
        >
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <p class="m-0 text-[12px] leading-[1.6] text-fg-muted">
      What the other two apps do is from their vendors' own pages, as they read on October 21, 2026.
      Drakar is not affiliated with Anthropic or OpenAI.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
